more important contention than the contention that our values are somehow
"true". Now don't go jump all over me for this paragraph; it's just a
footnote, really. I'm not prepared to defend any of it. And no, I'm not a 
moral relativist. I haven't committed to one side or the other of that 
particular question yet.  ;-)

One last thing: you could at least concede that PCR at least admits that
rationality is both possible and desirable, which puts it head and
shoulders above such nonsense as Rorty. Head and shoulders and torso and
thigh, actually. Some of your rhetoric sounds as if you're classing
Bartley and Rorty in the same school.




